00:49:03.060 --> 00:49:08.100
Despite Gladys' impressive victory, the Mayo Clinic study had been a portent of what was to come.

00:49:08.680 --> 00:49:13.640
By the summer of 1995, many more scientific studies had made it into print.

00:49:13.880 --> 00:49:21.430
This study failed to demonstrate an association between silicone breast implantation and the subsequent development of scleroderma.

00:49:21.950 --> 00:49:30.000
These data failed to support the hypothesis that augmentation mammoplasty with silicone gel-filled prostheses is a risk factor for the development of scleroderma.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:35.860
No cases of scleroderma or lupus were found, and the incidence of arthritis was not significantly different.

00:49:36.000 --> 00:49:37.620
The studies were remarkably consistent.

00:49:38.430 --> 00:49:43.490
This study found no statistically significant association between silicone breast implants and scleroderma.

00:49:43.830 --> 00:49:45.710
No association was seen between...

00:49:45.710 --> 00:49:49.370
Their conclusions were in total conflict with what was happening in the courts.

00:49:50.310 --> 00:49:51.890
This study found no evidence that women...

00:49:51.890 --> 00:49:57.630
While such studies did not exclude the possibility of a small association for perhaps a tiny subset of women,

00:49:57.970 --> 00:50:00.000
They effectively ruled out a large

00:50:00.120 --> 00:50:07.830
association between breast implants and connective tissue disease. June 1995

00:50:07.830 --> 00:50:11.960
researchers at the Harvard Medical School reported perhaps the best study

00:50:11.960 --> 00:50:17.150
so far in the New England Journal of Medicine. They too could find no

00:50:17.150 --> 00:50:23.120
