00:51:04.440 --> 00:51:09.100
published in this week's Journal of the American Medical Association. But the

00:51:09.100 --> 00:51:13.430
authors claim the increased risk is too small to mean anything, as the study is

00:51:13.430 --> 00:51:19.200
based on questionnaires that women filled in after 1992. The authors say the

00:51:19.200 --> 00:51:25.830
